arm64: dts: mediatek: add the mt6797 M4U node

Address 0x10205000 and IRQ 156 taken from the vendor 3.18 device tree
(arch/arm64/boot/dts/mt6797.dts, node m4u@10205000).

Only larb0 is listed in mediatek,larbs: it is the only larb this tree
instantiates and the whole display pipeline sits behind it. larb0 and
smi_common are already enabled by the board DTS.

Deliberately no clocks/clock-names: mt6797 has no infracfg M4U gate,
which is why mt6797_data omits HAS_BCLK.

This node alone changes nothing about how the display reaches memory.
The larb keeps every port in MMU bypass until a master actually attaches
to the IOMMU, so with no "iommus" property on any display component this
is inert by construction — which is the point. It lands first, on its
own, so that "the M4U probes cleanly and the panel is unaffected" is a
result rather than an assumption. Wiring the display's iommus properties
is a separate change.
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797.dtsi
@@ -497,6 +497,35 @@
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 	/*
+	 * M4U (MediaTek Multimedia Memory Management Unit) — the IOMMU in
+	 * front of the multimedia masters. Address 0x10205000 and IRQ 156
+	 * from the vendor 3.18 DT (arch/arm64/boot/dts/mt6797.dts,
+	 * node m4u@10205000); the address is the same one MT8173 uses, which
+	 * is consistent with them being the same generation.
+	 *
+	 * Why this matters beyond "the IOMMU is missing": without it
+	 * mediatek-drm can only scan out physically contiguous memory
+	 * (mtk_gem_prime_import_sg_table rejects any scattered sg_table), so
+	 * a panfrost-rendered buffer can never be handed to the display and
+	 * every GPU-composited pixel goes through a CPU copy. See B-39.
+	 *
+	 * Only larb0 is listed: it is the only larb this tree instantiates
+	 * and the whole display pipeline is behind it. Adding larb1..6 needs
+	 * their nodes first.
+	 *
+	 * Deliberately NO clocks/clock-names: mt6797 has no infracfg M4U
+	 * gate (mt6797_data omits HAS_BCLK for the same reason).
+	 */
+	m4u: iommu@10205000 {
+		compatible = "mediatek,mt6797-m4u";
+		reg = <0 0x10205000 0 0x1000>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 156 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		mediatek,infracfg = <&infrasys>;
+		mediatek,larbs = <&larb0>;
+		#iommu-cells = <1>;
+	};
+
+	/*
 	 * SMI common (Streaming Memory Interface shared bus arbiter).
 	 * Address 0x14022000 confirmed from vendor kernel DTB embedded in
 	 * planet/kali_boot.img (node smi_common@14022000).
